            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-0",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xxl",
            "max_width_desktop": "1096px",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Image_Ratio_Keeper_7928fce2-7bf3-4653-998c-c118b0173fe0.png",
            "image_desktop": "shopify://shop_images/Image_Ratio_Keeper_7928fce2-7bf3-4653-998c-c118b0173fe0.png",
            "caption": "",
            "caption_style": "p6",
            "product": "classic-pro-cp7i",
            "product_image_override": "shopify://shop_images/Classic_Pro_CP7i.png"
          }
        },
        "text_e9yarP": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-md",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-lg",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-0",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "95ch",
            "richtext": "<h4>Why air quality matters</h4><p></p><p>Did you know more than 100 million Americans experience allergies, and 27 million live with asthma? Additionally, people spend 90% of their time indoors, where air can be 2-5 times more polluted than outdoor air. That makes effective air purification essential for those living with asthma or allergies.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
        "text_Ub47yL": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-md",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-0",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "95ch",
            "richtext": "<h4>What Asthma and Allergy Friendly™ Certification Means</h4><p></p><p>The Asthma and Allergy Friendly™ Certification isn’t just a logo—it’s a sign of trust. It means that the Classic Pro CP7i has been third-party tested by independent medical experts who evaluate the product based on its ability to reduce airborne allergens, such as dust, pollen, pet dander, and smoke. These allergens are known triggers for asthma and allergies, and the certification ensures that the product is scientifically proven to address those concerns.</p><p></p><p>Many products on the market make claims about helping with asthma and allergies, but without proper testing, these claims can be misleading or even dangerous. False advertising about a product’s effectiveness can lead health complications for those who rely on the product for relief.</p><p></p><p>For example, using an air purifier that isn’t actually capable of removing harmful allergens may lead to a worsening of asthma symptoms, triggering allergic reactions, or even exacerbating respiratory issues.</p><p></p><p>With the Asthma and Allergy Friendly™ Certification, Blueair offers you the peace of mind that our Classic Pro Air Purifier has been rigorously tested to meet high standards of allergen reduction. You don’t have to rely on unverified marketing claims or guesswork—we’ve done the hard work to ensure that our air purifier actually does what it says. This certification is proof that the Classic Pro is truly effective in helping to tackle asthma and allergy issues.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
